# Line endings: LF in the repository AND in the working tree, on every
# platform. This matches `.editorconfig`'s `end_of_line = lf`, which has
# declared LF for the whole repo since it was added.
#
# Why this file has to say it: without a `text` attribute git stores whatever
# bytes the authoring tool happened to write, and this repo has
# `core.autocrlf=false`, so nothing normalises. The result was 1089 CRLF files
# beside 19 LF ones -- and, worse, a file rewritten by a different tool flips
# wholesale, so git reports a one-line change as a full-file rewrite. That is
# the diff noise this fixes.
#
# `eol=lf` (rather than bare `text=auto`) also pins the *working tree*, so a
# Windows checkout matches what `.editorconfig` tells the editor to write and
# the two can't disagree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ── Binary assets: never touch ────────────────────────────────────────
# `text=auto` already spares these via content detection, but detection reads
# only the first few KB, so declare the ones we ship explicitly. The Live2D
# rig formats are listed for the same reason `.editorconfig` lists them: the
# assets live outside git today (`data/`), and a future `git add` of a rig
# must not be corrupted by normalisation.
*.png   -text
*.ico   -text
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.safetensors -text
*.moc3  -text
*.moc   -text
*.cdi3.json -text
*.wav   -text
*.mp3   -text
*.ogg   -text
*.woff  -text
*.woff2 -text
*.ttf   -text

# ── Files where LF is load-bearing, not cosmetic ──────────────────────
# Redundant under the blanket rule above, and kept anyway: these are the ones
# whose breakage is silent and remote. A CRLF `entrypoint.sh` copied into a
# Linux image fails at boot with `/usr/bin/env: 'sh\r': No such file or
# directory` -- see docs/docker.md. Spelling them out means a future edit to
# the blanket rule can't quietly reintroduce that.
*.sh    text eol=lf
docker/entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf

# ── Generated / vendored: keep out of diffs and merges ────────────────
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
web/package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
web/src-tauri/Cargo.lock -diff linguist-generated
requirements.lock -diff
web/public/live2d/*.min.js -diff linguist-vendored
